"""Sector breadth, thrusts and leader flags for the website: the rules of the TradingView indicator
"Sector & Leaders v2.0", run on NSE's industry classification and on a universe of stocks rebuilt every month
(universe.py), and the figures of the Nov 2026 study (NSE data 2016-2026, 46 groups, delisted stocks included).

For every NSE industry (or sector group of small industries) and every trading day:
  breadth       % of its counted stocks closing above their 9, 20 and 50-day EMA (8+ stocks with data)
  index         equal-weighted index of the counted stocks' daily returns (a move of 50%+ ignored, 6+ stocks)
  higher-low    while the index's 60-day low is at most 15 sessions old: % of stocks that held a higher low ON that
  share         low day (own 60-day low 10+ sessions earlier, 3%+ below that day's close); carried 30 sessions
  state         Neutral, Washout, Thrust C, Thrust CAP, Confirmed, Fading
and for every counted stock: the leader flag (52-week closing high while the index is 15%+ / 10%+ below its 52-week
high, live 60 sessions), the 6-month return quartile inside the group and the bottom timing.

The views (board, industry, stock) return JSON-ready dicts. The wording describes; it never says what to do.
"""
